<urn:anqr:profile-foundation-binding:2> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A port is bound because an ANQR requirement demands it. Binding a port names a required capability shape; it names no provider, and no provider fulfilling it is an ANQR product concept." <urn:anqr:graph:profile-revision-2> .
<urn:anqr:profile-foundation-binding:2> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The binding names the foundation authority it resolves against by path rather than importing it. A product overlay that imported the foundation would absorb every core contract and lose the isolation that keeps unrelated core movement from staling it." <urn:anqr:graph:profile-revision-2> .
<urn:anqr:profile-foundation-binding:2> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The dependency closure is the transitive resource closure of these seeds, not the whole foundation. Movement in a foundation resource outside that closure leaves this profile current, and that is the property the binding exists to make true rather than to assert." <urn:anqr:graph:profile-revision-2> .
